base='/sources/clock-plant-v0.1/';pdf=C/names[0]
content='''<div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">20 October 2026 UTC · CPC v0.1</div><h1>The clock must fit the physical plant.</h1><p class="lede">A component audit exposes a compatibility gate: slower filtered acquisition can require a substantially slower canonical LC plant.</p></div>
<aside class="callout"><strong>Derived conditional · Hardware HOLD · Physical promotion 0</strong><p>Two elementary theorems establish clock–plant compatibility and filtered-history error. Ten exact controls and alternative SAC/FCAL budget replays pass. Supplier specifications are not measurements of an assembled apparatus; independent review remains pending.</p></aside>
<div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="PDF_PATH">Read four-page theorem and audit PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="ZIP_PATH">Download source package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="PLAN_PATH">Open identification plan</a></div>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>Slowing the clock is not a free adjustment.</h2><p>For each physical canonical pair, normalized plant coefficients satisfy αβ=t₀²/(LC). Their smallest possible common maximum is t₀/√(LC), achieved by balanced flux–charge scales. The inherited λ≤1 requirement therefore needs t₀≤min √(LC).</p><p>The timing allocation gives the other side: t₀ must be at least 400000 times the largest of output period, filter-history moment plus electronics latency, and actuator time constant. Both sides must hold on calibrated intervals.</p><p>The audited averaging-mode spacing yields a lower clock of 2048/5 seconds under this allocation. Every pair would then require LC≥4194304/25 seconds squared. A declared LC≤1 second squared envelope has no overlap. This is a restriction on the stated contract, not a universal impossibility result.</p></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>A filtered sample contains history.</h2><p>The readout theorem bounds error by state speed times the absolute first age moment of the filter, plus bounded raw error times the absolute coefficient sum. Signed filter weights can have zero signed group delay and still carry nonzero history error.</p><p>Filter mode, coefficients, aperture times, startup tails, channel skew and output availability must be recorded. Typical RMS noise and an advertised bit count do not establish the required simultaneous reconstruction bound.</p></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>A revised accuracy allocation passes mathematically.</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Alternative supplied quantity</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Input reconstruction bound ν</td><td>1/100000</td></tr>
<tr><td>Complete command error q</td><td>1/25000</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tracking bound</td><td>29383/16000000</td></tr>
<tr><td>Total continuous residual</td><td>149383/16000000 = 0.0093364375</td></tr>
<tr><td>Slack below 1/100</td><td>10617/16000000</td></tr>
</tbody></table><p>The alternative preserves the earlier conditional Gauss fault gaps and preload tolerance. It extends the valid earlier allocation; it does not replace its historical record. Actual noise, affine errors, drift, reference and driver errors must fit the remaining allowances.</p><p>The initial screen covers AD5791B, LTC2500-32 and an ADS127L21 alternative. All are candidates. Exact conditions and manufacturer links are in the audit; no part is admitted or selected for purchase.</p></div></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>The required identification records are explicit.</h2><p>First return actual L, C, loading, canonical action and energy scales, and a nonempty clock interval. Next freeze the converter history and timing. Then provide traceable static calibration, simultaneous noise bounds, and independent actuator output and derivative records.</p><p>The actuator test must bound rₐ=(physical output derivative)/(physical pole)+output−held command on every relevant held segment, including one-sided transitions and glitches. Finite samples require a separate regularity and coverage certificate.</p><p>Release tracking, prehistory speed, range, slew and work remain required. Blinded nominal and fault runs follow only after the premises and attributable non-constructor review are recorded. No experiment has been performed.</p><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/sampled-actuator/">Read the sampled-actuator theorem →</a></div></section>'''
content=content.replace('PDF_PATH',base+pdf.name).replace('ZIP_PATH',base+release.name).replace('PLAN_PATH',base+'IDENTIFICATION_PLAN_v0.1.json')
template=(D/'evidence/index.html').read_text()
page=re.sub(r'<main id="main">.*?</main>',lambda _:'<main id="main">'+content+'</main>',template,flags=re.S).replace('<title>Evidence · Unified Dynamics</title>','<title>Clock and Plant Compatibility · Unified Dynamics</title>')
p=D/'evidence/clock-plant';p.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);(p/'index.html').write_text(page)
card='''<article class="claim" id="clock-plant-v01"><div class="eyebrow">20 October 2026 UTC · Clock–plant compatibility 0.1</div><h2>Converter selection now has a clock–plant compatibility gate</h2><p>The exact LC identity and a filtered-readout theorem prevent treating slower acquisition as a free remedy. A revised input/command allocation passes the prior Gauss budget, while hardware admission remains HOLD. Ten exact controls and inherited-budget replays pass.</p><p>Four-page theorem and preliminary supplier audit; identification plan OPEN; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/clock-plant/">Read theorem, audit and identification requirements →</a></article>'''
for rel,marker in [('updates/index.html','<article class="claim"'),('evidence/index.html','<section class="chapter"')]:
    p=D/rel;s=p.read_text();assert 'id="clock-plant-v01"' not in s;i=s.index(marker);p.write_text(s[:i]+card+s[i:])
p=D/'evidence/sampled-actuator/index.html';s=p.read_text();i=s.index('<section class="chapter"')
note='<aside class="callout"><strong>Next milestone: physical clock and plant compatibility</strong><p>The component screen adds the LC clock-product restriction, filtered-history error and an alternative accuracy allocation.</p><a href="/evidence/clock-plant/">Read the clock–plant theorem and audit →</a></aside>'
p.write_text(s[:i]+note+s[i:])
p=D/'papers/index.html';s=p.read_text();i=s.index('<article class="paper-row" id="sampled-actuator-v01">')
paper='<article class="paper-row" id="clock-plant-v01"><div class="paper-number">CPC</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem and preliminary component audit · 0.1</span><h2>Clock–plant compatibility and filtered readout</h2><p>Exact LC clock-product identity, absolute filter-history bound, conservative certificate obstruction, revised error allocation and identification plan. Four pages; ten exact controls and inherited-budget replay. Hardware HOLD; review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="'+base+pdf.name+'">Read theorem and audit PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/clock-plant/">Read the compatibility gate →</a></div></div></article>'
p.write_text(s[:i]+paper+s[i:])
p=D/'assets/sources.json';sources=json.loads(p.read_text());assert not any(x['id']=='CPC01' for x in sources)
sources.append({'id':'CPC01','title':'Clock–plant compatibility and filtered readout v0.1','group':'Theorem manuscripts','status':'DERIVED CONDITIONAL / CANDIDATE COMPONENT ROUTE / HARDWARE HOLD / REVIEW PENDING','note':'Exact LC clock-product identity, filtered-history theorem, conservative certificate floor, manufacturer screen and alternate residual allocation. Physical promotion 0.','url':'/evidence/clock-plant/','local':base+pdf.name,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(pdf.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'size_bytes':pdf.stat().st_size,'content':'CPC v0.1: alpha*beta=t0^2/(LC); optimal canonical scaling minimizes scalar plant bound to max t0/sqrt(LC). Under inherited lambda<=1 the physical clock cannot exceed min sqrt(LC). Timing requirements supply a lower bound, so their interval must overlap. Filter readout uses absolute first moment and absolute coefficient sum; signed group delay alone is insufficient. A clock-independent floor obstructs only the existing conservative controller certificate, not actual physical performance. Alternate nu=1/100000 and q=1/25000 give total residual149383/16000000 <1/100 and preserve prior Gauss-prefix tolerances. Manufacturer documents support a preliminary component screen, not apparatus observations. Frozen identification plan requires actual plant/scales, filter timestamps, calibrated accuracy, independent actuator residual and review. Hardware HOLD, no experiment, no full-campaign or physical admission.'})
p.write_text(json.dumps(sources,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
print(json.dumps({'source_id':'CPC01','page':'/evidence/clock-plant/','release_bytes':release.stat().st_size}))
